IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dnc-consumer`

-- Do Not Call Register Act 2006 (Cth), ss 5, 11, 14, 15, 17, 24, 25, 30, 34, 39, Schedules 1, 2 and 3 cl 4 -- worked cases
-- from the seat of the consumer called by telemarketers.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, an ACMA determination or the regulations (none was deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_do-not-call-register-act-2006_baseline.py).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe): Chloe, 21, gets marketing calls and texts in
-- July 2024 and asks whether she can stop them (c044). The scenario gives no dates of registration or of calls, and no
-- callers; the day she registers (2 July 2024), the calls and the callers are the encoder's. Fixtures not named for the
-- event are invented for the case.

