§ `ss 14, 15, 17 -- can I register my number, and for how long (c044)`

-- c044: Chloe's mobile is used for private purposes, so it may go on the Register.
#ASSERT `Is my number eligible for the Register` `Chloe's mobile, registered on 2 July 2024 (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my number eligible for the Register` `a tradesperson's mobile used mainly for the business`)

-- c044: Chloe holds the mobile account herself; a flatmate who was never nominated in writing may not apply.
#ASSERT `May I apply to register the number` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I apply to register the number` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply to register the number` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 17: from entry, indefinitely, unless removed; 30 years on it is still in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my number registered on` `Chloe's mobile, registered on 2 July 2024 (c044)` 20240701)
#ASSERT `Is my number registered on` `Chloe's mobile, registered on 2 July 2024 (c044)` 20240702
#ASSERT `Is my number registered on` `Chloe's mobile, registered on 2 July 2024 (c044)` 20540702
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my number registered on` `a number entered in 2010 and removed under an ACMA determination in 2020` 20200601)
#ASSERT `Is my number registered on` `the same number re-registered on 1 March 2024` 20240401

§ `s 5 -- is it a telemarketing call (c044)`

-- c044: the sales call is a telemarketing call; the text message is not a voice call (Spam Act 2003).
#ASSERT `Is it a telemarketing call` `a telco's sales call to Chloe on 20 August 2024 (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a telemarketing call` `a marketing text message to Chloe (c044)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a telemarketing call` `a research survey call with no selling or fund-raising purpose`)
#ASSERT `Is it a telemarketing call` `a registered charity asking Chloe for donations`

-- APP 7.8 bridge, consistent with the Privacy Act baseline: APP 7 gives way for the call, not because of this Act for the text.
#ASSERT `Does this Act reach the call` `a telco's sales call to Chloe on 20 August 2024 (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this Act reach the call` `a marketing text message to Chloe (c044)`)

§ `Schedule 1 -- which callers are exempt`

#ASSERT NOT (`Is the caller exempt` `a telco's sales call to Chloe on 20 August 2024 (c044)`)
#ASSERT `Is the caller exempt` `a registered charity asking Chloe for donations`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the caller exempt` `a registered charity selling another firm's energy plans`)
#ASSERT `Is the caller exempt` `a registered political party fund-raising`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the caller exempt` `a registered political party selling merchandise it supplies, not fund-raising`)
#ASSERT `Is the caller exempt` `Chloe's old university selling alumni insurance it supplies`

§ `Schedule 2 -- did I consent`

-- cl 3: express consent with no period stated lapses at the end of 3 months beginning on 15 May 2024 (14 August).
#ASSERT `Was my express consent in force on` `express consent on 15 May 2024, no period stated` 20240814
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my express consent in force on` `express consent on 15 May 2024, no period stated` 20240815)
#ASSERT `Was my express consent in force on` `express consent on 15 May 2024 until 31 December 2024` 20240820
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my express consent in force on` `express consent on 15 May 2024, indefinitely, withdrawn before the call` 20240820)

#ASSERT `Did I consent to the call` `consent inferred from Chloe's dealings as the telco's current customer` 20240820
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I consent to the call` `nothing but Chloe's number being published` 20240820)
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I consent to the call` `express consent on 15 May 2024, no period stated` 20240820)

§ `s 11 -- was the call to me allowed (c044)`

-- c044: once Chloe's number is registered, the telco's sales call without her consent contravenes s 11(1).
#ASSERT (`Was the call allowed` `a telco's sales call to Chloe on 20 August 2024 (c044)` `no consent` FALSE) EQUALS `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it`
#ASSERT (`Was the call allowed` `the same call on 1 July 2024, before she registered (c044)` `no consent` FALSE) EQUALS `allowed: my number was not on the Register on the day of the call`
#ASSERT (`Was the call allowed` `a marketing text message to Chloe (c044)` `no consent` FALSE) EQUALS `allowed: it is not a telemarketing call under this Act`
#ASSERT (`Was the call allowed` `a registered charity asking Chloe for donations` `no consent` FALSE) EQUALS `allowed: the caller is exempt under Schedule 1`
#ASSERT (`Was the call allowed` `a telco's sales call to Chloe on 20 August 2024 (c044)` `consent inferred from Chloe's dealings as the telco's current customer` FALSE) EQUALS `allowed: I or my nominee consented`
#ASSERT (`Was the call allowed` `a telco's sales call to Chloe on 20 August 2024 (c044)` `nothing but Chloe's number being published` TRUE) EQUALS `forbidden by s 11(1), but the caller has a defence under s 11(3), (4) or (5)`

§ `ss 24, 30, 34 -- what can I do about it (c044)`

#ASSERT (`What can I do about the call` `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it` FALSE FALSE 20240820 20241001) EQUALS `I have no application of my own: only the ACMA may seek a civil penalty or an injunction (ss 24, 34)`
#ASSERT (`What can I do about the call` `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it` TRUE TRUE 20240820 20260101) EQUALS `I may apply to the court for compensation for my loss or damage (s 30)`
#ASSERT (`What can I do about the call` `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it` TRUE TRUE 20240820 20300820) EQUALS `too late: more than 6 years have passed since the call (s 30(4))`
#ASSERT (`What can I do about the call` `allowed: the caller is exempt under Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE 20240820 20241001) EQUALS `nothing under this Act: the call was not forbidden`

§ `s 25, Schedule 3 -- what the caller can be made to pay`

#ASSERT (`What is the most the caller can be ordered to pay for one call` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`What is the most the caller can be ordered to pay for one call` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT (`What is the most the caller can be ordered to pay for one call` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 20

